From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert Wojciechowski <24755+wojo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:01:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] glm cuda: --learn-conversations keeps every rank's part of a
 kept state on disk (ashhart/TensorFold#1411)

A backport of ashhart/TensorFold#1411 (head d903d8597, on main a757420c6) to this stack (f350cd3e + 0001-0108).
With --learn-conversations, GLM-5.3-Flash's kept prompt states go to the rows store on disk, every rank's part,
so a conversation resumes from disk after its RAM copy is evicted or the server restarts. Off by default and
unchanged when the flag is unset.

- cuda_disk_image: a kept state's disk image on one rank: the words (format, position, head rows, ring bases,
  KDA copy bits), the KDA prefix, each DSA layer's latent rows, scales and pooled keys by position, the rings
  and pools in progress, the head's caches at a whole verify window, then the tail. Copies run a page of the
  lease at a time: 0015's device pages, then its pinned host pages.
- cuda_disk_ranks + cuda_follow's disk step: rank 0's engine thread leases, fills, reads and seals each rank's
  copy through the follow link. The store's image is rank 0's image followed by each other rank's prefix; the
  rest is the same bytes on every rank, checked at start by the identity probe.
- cuda_snapshots: blankAs/seal. A disk read's blank state is refused by restore until its seal checks the
  words (head rows within the verify window, ring bases that hold the state's rows, copy bits).
- native: the disk store attaches for GLM; --spill-gib and --checkpoint-slots are refused for GLM, as
  --learn-conversations alone keeps its states.
- rows: a pool that reuses spare storage reads a disk state into it; a trimming pool stays within its budget.

On this stack:
- The lease is 0015's two tiers. A host page copies with a memcpy, a device page with cuMemcpyDtoH/HtoD.
- Beside DFlash2 a kept state's head holds no rows, and the image carries no drafter ring. A state read from
  disk restores with DFlash2 restarted at the mark, as TF_GLM_SNAP_DRAFTER=0 does for a RAM state.
- Not carried over from upstream: TF_GLM_KV_SHARE's refusal (no such switch here) and #2207's identity profile.
- Tests take window_rows 16 (0039) and index_ring 8,192 (0094), and the round trip runs on a device-only pool
  and on one whose lease runs onto host pages.

Original commits by Robert Wojciechowski (GitHub @wojo, X @rwojo) in ashhart/TensorFold#1411.
